'\" t
.TH APP_TOP_MONITORING 1 "@NEO_MAN_DATE@" "app_top_monitoring @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
app_top_monitoring \- a top\-like Linux process monitor with remote monitoring, deployment, capture, logging and alerting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B app_top_monitoring
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATTERN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B app_top_monitoring
displays live process information from
.I /proc
in a
.BR top (1)-like
table, sortable and filterable, with three extra capabilities beyond a
typical process monitor: it can attach to a
.B remote
host over SSH or Telnet and display
.I that
host's processes instead (or deploy itself there first over FTP/TFTP), it
can
.B capture
a timed series of system\-wide samples to a CSV file and an interactive
HTML chart report, and it can watch CPU/memory usage for a
.B sustained
threshold breach and raise an alert.
.PP
A bare positional
.I PATTERN
argument is shorthand for an include filter: it is matched against each
process's command name and full command line (case\-insensitive
substring).
.PP
A separate Qt GUI application,
.BR app_top_monitoring_qt (1),
shares this same backend and adds live graphs, a native capture viewer,
a system tray icon, and point\-and\-click process actions.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Display and refresh
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " \fISECONDS\fR
Refresh interval (default 2.0). Also the per\-sample interval for
.BR \-\-capture .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-long\-args
Show the full command line instead of just the command name.
.TP
.B \-\-swap
Show the swap column.
.TP
.B \-\-io
Show I/O read/write rate columns.
.TP
.B \-\-threads
Show the thread\-count column.
.TP
.B \-\-start\-time
Show each process's start time.
.TP
.B \-\-elapsed
Show each process's elapsed runtime.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-reverse
Reverse the current sort order.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-limit " " \fICOUNT\fR
Only display the first N processes after sorting (0 = unlimited).
.SS Filtering
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exclude " " \fIPATTERN\fR
Exclude processes whose command name or command line contains
.I PATTERN
(case\-insensitive substring). Exclusions take priority over include
patterns.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pid " " \fIPID\fR[,\fIPID\fR...]
Only show these PIDs.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-ppid " " \fIPPID\fR[,\fIPPID\fR...]
Only show children of these PPIDs.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fR
Local mode: filter to this user's processes. Remote mode: the login
username instead.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-state " " \fISTATES\fR
Only show processes in these states, e.g.
.IR R,S,D,T,Z,I .
.TP
.B \-\-cpu\-threshold \fIPERCENT\fR
Hide processes below this CPU%.
.TP
.B \-\-ram\-mb \fIMB\fR
Hide processes below this RSS.
.TP
.B \-\-ram\-percent \fIPERCENT\fR
Hide processes below this memory%.
.SS Sorting
.TP
.B \-\-sort \fIMODE\fR
One of
.BR cpu ", " mem ", " pid ", " rss ", " io_read ", " io_write
(default
.BR cpu ).
.SS Execution mode
.TP
.BR \-1 ", " \-\-once
Run a single scan and exit.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-batch
Non\-interactive batch mode (also implied by \-\-csv/\-\-json).
.TP
.B \-\-csv
CSV output instead of the interactive table.
.TP
.B \-\-json
JSON output instead of the interactive table.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable terminal colors.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SS Remote connectivity (SSH/Telnet/FTP/TFTP)
.TP
.B \-\-protocol \fIPROTOCOL\fR
One of
.BR local ", " ssh ", " telnet ", " ftp ", " tftp
(default
.BR local ).
.TP
.B \-\-host \fIADDRESS\fR
Remote host address. Required for any non\-local protocol.
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIPASSWORD\fR
Login password (telnet/ftp only; ssh uses key\-based auth exclusively).
.TP
.B \-\-port \fINUMBER\fR
Override the protocol's default port (22 ssh, 23 telnet, 21 ftp, 69
tftp).
.TP
.B \-\-identity \fIPATH\fR
SSH private key (optional; ssh only).
.TP
.B \-\-remote\-bin \fINAME\fR
Name or path of
.B app_top_monitoring
on the remote host (ssh/telnet monitoring).
.TP
.B \-\-local\-file \fIPATH\fR
File to upload (ftp/tftp deploy).
.TP
.B \-\-remote\-file \fINAME\fR
Destination filename on the remote host (ftp/tftp deploy; defaults to
the local filename).
.PP
.B \-\-capture
combined with a non\-local
.B \-\-protocol
is rejected with an error.
.SS Capture (time\-series + chart report)
.TP
.B \-\-capture
Capture until Ctrl+C.
.TP
.B \-\-capture=\fISECONDS\fR
Capture for
.I SECONDS
then stop automatically. Note the
.BR = ;
.B \-\-capture 30
does not work as a duration.
.TP
.B \-\-capture\-output \fIBASEPATH\fR
Base path for the two output files (no extension); default
.IR capture_<unix\-timestamp> .
.SS Logging
.TP
.B \-\-log\-file \fIPATH\fR
Append timestamped log entries to
.IR PATH .
Disabled by default; stdout/stderr behave exactly as before. Records
refresh errors, remote connection attempts/failures, and capture
start/stop, formatted as
.IR "[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS] [LEVEL] message" .
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level \fILEVEL\fR
Minimum severity recorded: one of
.BR error ", " warn ", " info ", " debug
(default
.BR info ).
.SS Threshold alerting
.TP
.B \-\-alert\-cpu \fIPERCENT\fR
Alert when system\-wide CPU% stays above this value. Unset/0 disables
this check.
.TP
.B \-\-alert\-mem \fIPERCENT\fR
Alert when system\-wide memory% stays above this value. Unset/0
disables this check.
.TP
.B \-\-alert\-duration \fISECONDS\fR
How long a threshold must be continuously exceeded before it fires
(default 5).
.TP
.B \-\-alert\-notify
Send a desktop notification via
.BR notify-send (1)
(if installed) when an alert fires.
.TP
.B \-\-alert\-webhook \fIURL\fR
POST a small JSON payload to
.I URL
via
.BR curl (1)
(if installed) when an alert fires.
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
Available in the default interactive table mode (not
\-\-once/\-\-batch/\-\-csv/\-\-json):
.TS
tab(:);
l l.
q:Quit
c:Sort by CPU
m:Sort by memory
p:Sort by PID
+:Increase refresh interval
\-:Decrease refresh interval
r:Force refresh
v:Reverse sort order
.TE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, and (when alerting is configured) no alert fired during the
run.
.TP
.B 1
A fatal error occurred (bad arguments, failed to read
.IR /proc ,
remote connection failure, deploy failure, and similar).
.TP
.B 2
Success, but a
\-\-alert\-cpu/\-\-alert\-mem
threshold fired (or was still active) at exit \- see
.B Threshold alerting
above. Only meaningful when alerting is configured; otherwise this
exit status is not used.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Watch local processes, sorted by memory:
.B app_top_monitoring \-\-sort mem
.TP
One JSON snapshot for scripting:
.B app_top_monitoring \-\-once \-\-json
.TP
Monitor a remote card over SSH:
.B app_top_monitoring \-\-protocol ssh \-\-host 10.0.0.5 \-u admin
.TP
Capture 60 seconds of system load with post\-mortem logging:
.B app_top_monitoring \-\-capture=60 \-\-log\-file /var/log/app_top_monitoring.log
.TP
Alert if CPU stays above 90% for a minute, notifying and exiting 2:
.B app_top_monitoring \-\-alert\-cpu 90 \-\-alert\-duration 60 \-\-alert\-notify
.SH FILES
.TP
.I VERSION
Single source of truth for the version reported by \-\-version and this
manual page.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR top (1),
.BR ps (1),
.BR notify-send (1),
.BR curl (1)
.PP
Full documentation, including the Qt GUI guide and remote\-testing
setup, ships alongside the source in
.IR docs/ .
.SH AUTHOR
See the project's README and CONTRIBUTING documentation.
